  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.
    MemberName: FullBodyCalibration
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - good
    - BasisLocalPlayer.Instance.LocalBoneDriver.SimulateAndApplyWithoutLerp(BasisLocalPlayer.Instance
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Builds a tracker\u2192role assignment from the player's T-pose constellation
      alone.\n The avatar is no longer the source of truth for \"where should this
      tracker be\";\n instead the HMD defines a body frame and each tracker is classified
      by its\n height-above-floor and lateral offset, normalized to the calibrated
      player eye\n height. ComputeHints below still consults the avatar (chest/hips
      reference\n rotations), but the role-matching pass itself is avatar-independent
      \u2014 so the\n same trackers map the same way whether the user wears a child
      avatar or a\n three-meter giant."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
