  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.
    MemberName: TryGetCalibrationVisualizationFrame
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 4
    ParamNames:
    - bodyOrigin
    - bodyRotation
    - eyeHeight
    - priors
    ParamDocs:
    - 'World-space anchor: HMD position projected to the floor.'
    - 'Body forward rotation: HMD facing flattened to horizontal.'
    - Eye height (meters), used to convert ratio-space priors to world distances.
    - Per-role priors. Snapshot priors when a calibration has run, default-armReach
      priors otherwise.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Returns the body-frame anchor and per-role priors used to render\n
      calibration acceptance-region gizmos. Always prefers a live HMD pose\n so the
      regions track wherever the player is now (rather than freezing\n at the last
      calibration snapshot). Falls back to the snapshot frame if\n no HMD device
      is available, or returns false if there's no usable\n frame source at all."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
