  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.
    MemberName: DetermineAction
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - connector
    - null
    ParamDocs:
    - The bundle metadata for the loaded avatar.
    - "The player's cached PerformanceInfo\n from the last load \u2014 what was actually
      trimmed on disk."
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Decide what the settings bridge should do with a player after a limit\n
      change. Compares each category's currently-kept count (derived from\n metadata
      + stored trim counts) against what the new limits would keep\n and picks the
      cheapest correct response:\n\n   \u2022 ReconcileAction.None \u2014 no category
      would change and\n     the hard-block flag didn't flip. Skip the player entirely.\n  
      \u2022 ReconcileAction.TrimInPlace \u2014 every change tightens\n     an existing
      count. Destroy the extras on the live avatar; no reload,\n     no bundle I/O,
      no setup pass.\n   \u2022 ReconcileAction.Reload \u2014 a trim category relaxed\n    
      (destroyed components need to come back), the limit got disabled,\n     or
      the hard-block flag flipped. Full `ReloadAvatar` required."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.
    MemberName: TrimExcessComponents
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - root
    ParamDocs:
    - The instantiated avatar root GameObject.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Per-category classification step shared by DetermineAction.\n Returns
      false when the category needs a restore (new target > currently\n kept), which
      forces the caller to pick ReconcileAction.Reload.\n Otherwise flips `anyTighten`
      to true if this category has\n components to destroy and returns true.\n\n
      `protectedCount` is the number of instances the runtime\n always keeps *and*
      ignores when counting against the limit. Animators use\n 1 for BasisAvatar.Animator,
      which the remote driver disables\n so it never ticks. The effective target
      becomes\n `min(original, limit + protectedCount)` \u2014 the user's cap applies
      only\n to the instances that are actually running."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
