  - TypeFullName: SMModuleAvatarLoadGates
    MemberName: SMModuleAvatarLoadGates
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Settings bridge that forwards the three avatar-load concurrency sliders
      into\n BasisAvatarFactory. Unlike the other SMModule classes, this one is not\n
      a BasisSettingsBase MonoBehaviour \u2014 it doesn't need to live on the\n BasisFramework
      prefab. It subscribes directly to\n BasisSettingsSystem.OnSettingChanged via
      a runtime-init hook, which\n means adding a new load-gate setting is a pure
      code change with no prefab edit."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: SMModuleAvatarPerformanceLimits
    MemberName: SMModuleAvatarPerformanceLimits
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Settings bridge that forwards the performance-limit sliders/toggles
      into\n BasisAvatarPerformanceLimits. Mirrors `SMModuleAvatarLoadGates`:\n subscribes
      once at runtime init, seeds the static state from the saved settings,\n and
      reacts to BasisSettingsSystem.OnSettingChanged.\n\n Setting values are applied
      immediately (cheap field writes), but the resulting\n avatar reload pass is
      debounced \u2014 rapid toggling would otherwise fire one full\n reconcile per
      click, and reconcile reloads every remote avatar in the room. The\n debounce
      collapses a burst of changes into a single reconcile after the user has\n settled,
      so flipping ten toggles in a second reloads each avatar once, not ten\n times."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
