  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.
    MemberName: FreezeLayoutSize
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (_layoutFrozen
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Freezes this descriptor's layout size so future text changes don't
      cascade\n layout rebuilds up through parent LayoutGroups. Works by:\n  1. Running
      ForceRebuildLayoutImmediate so the current natural size is captured.\n  2.
      Disabling every ContentSizeFitter in the subtree \u2014 each one would otherwise\n    
      recompute on every text change and re-dirty parents.\n  3. Pinning a LayoutElement.preferredHeight
      on the root so parent LayoutGroups\n     see a stable value (max of current
      natural height and minHeight).\n Call this AFTER the descriptor has been populated
      with its initial content.\n Pass a `minHeight` large enough to fit future content
      \u2014 once\n frozen, if text grows beyond this the overflow will be clipped."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
