    Summary: "Builds TMP font assets from OS-installed fonts and wires them up as\n
      global fallbacks so any TextMeshPro label falls through to a system\n font
      when its primary font doesn't have a glyph. This is how we get\n broad Unicode
      coverage (CJK, Cyrillic, Arabic, Devanagari, Thai\u2026)\n without having to
      ship every glyph inside a baked static atlas.\n\n Runs once before the first
      scene loads. Define\n `BASIS_DISABLE_TMP_FALLBACKS` to opt out."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.
    MemberName: InstallFallbacks
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (_installed
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Ordered candidates for each fallback slot. Names are OS font\n family
      names and are fed one-by-one to\n TMP_FontAsset.CreateFontAsset(string, string,
      int),\n which asks the underlying FontEngine to resolve the font file on\n
      the host OS. The first name that resolves wins. The list\n intentionally overlaps
      Windows / macOS / Linux / Android so a\n single array serves every platform."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
