    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Walks a per-script list of OS font candidates and adds the first installed\n
      match per script to the nameplate font's fallback list. This lets display\n
      names render glyphs the primary (Latin) font doesn't cover \u2014 Japanese,\n
      Korean, Chinese, Arabic, Thai, Hebrew, Devanagari \u2014 instead of silently\n
      dropping them. Scripts with no installed candidate degrade to \"no glyph\";\n
      no crash. Per-family dedupe avoids loading the same atlas twice when a\n font
      (e.g., Tahoma covers both Arabic and Hebrew) was added for an earlier\n script
      in the chain."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
