  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.UI.NamePlate.
    MemberName: CanCurrentlyBeHeard
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (!IsVisible
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Returns true when audio from this player is currently audible to the
      local\n user. Main-thread only \u2014 touches Unity components (audio source
      volume)."
    Remarks: "Covers every state that should prevent a talking pulse:\n face-visibility,
      failed-load pin, block state (local or remote temp),\n audio receiver presence,
      out-of-range (signalled by `HasAudioSource==false`,\n since Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.BasisAudioReceiver.StopAudio\n
      fires on the out-of-range transition), and individual-player mute\n (`audioSource.volume==0`,
      set by `ChangeRemotePlayersVolumeSettings`).\n Continuous audio streams from
      speakers the user can't hear will repeatedly\n fail this check and so never
      latch the pulse."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
