  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.SettingsProviderTrackerSettings
    MemberName: SettingsProviderTrackerSettings
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Settings tab that lists every connected full-body-eligible tracker
      and lets\n the user (a) link any two of them into a virtual midpoint pair and
      (b) force\n a body role on a tracker so calibration binds it without going
      through\n constellation discovery. The constellation classifier in\n BasisAvatarIKStageCalibration
      consumes both: pairings via BasisTrackerPairing,\n forced roles via BasisTrackerRoleOverride.\n\n
      Layout: a static intro + tuning section at the top (built once when the tab\n
      is created and bound to settings so values persist), then a dynamic list of\n
      per-tracker entries below \u2014 each entry has a \"linked with\" dropdown
      and a\n \"force role\" dropdown.\n\n Pairing/override-graph updates only refresh
      the *selected value* of each\n existing dropdown \u2014 they do NOT tear the
      dropdowns down. Tearing down a\n dropdown while the user is mid-click on one
      of its options destroys the\n GameObject the click is being routed to and makes
      the whole entry list\n flicker out. A full rebuild only happens when the set
      of eligible trackers\n actually changes (a tracker connected or disconnected)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
