    Summary: "Pulls SteamVR's grown recommended render target (which factors in the
      lens\n distortion overlap between eyes) and bakes it into XRSettings.eyeTextureResolutionScale\n
      once at SteamVR init. The OpenVR XR plugin allocates eye textures at Unity's\n
      default size \u2014 without this, Steam super-sampling and the per-headset
      native\n resolution are silently ignored. After this runs the URP renderScale
      slider\n behaves identically to OpenXR/Desktop: slider 1.0 = native recommended,\n
      slider X = X \xD7 native."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
