  - TypeFullName: BasisServerHandle.BasisServerInfoQuery
    MemberName: BasisServerInfoQuery
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Handles unconnected \"server info\" probes \u2014 the LiteNetLib UDP
      equivalent of a\n Minecraft server-list-ping. A client sends a tiny query packet
      to the server's\n listening port and gets back the public server name, current/max
      player count,\n MOTD, and the original nonce so the client can measure RTT.\n\n
      Wire format (little-endian):\n   Query:    [u32 ServerInfoQueryMagic][u16 protoVersion][u16
      nonce][padding \u2265 ServerInfoMinRequestBytes total]\n   Response: [u32 ServerInfoResponseMagic][u16
      protoVersion][u16 nonce]\n             [u16 online][u16 max][string name][string
      motd]\n\n DDoS protections:\n   1. Minimum request size \u2014 undersized packets
      (which is what a reflection\n      attacker would spoof to maximize amplification)
      are dropped before any work.\n      Clients pad their query so the response
      is never larger than the request,\n      so the amplification factor is < 1.\n  
      2. Global token bucket \u2014 caps the total responses-per-second the server\n     
      will emit, regardless of source. Bounds the worst-case outbound bandwidth\n     
      even if every protection above is bypassed.\n   3. Bounded per-IP throttle
      \u2014 one response per IP per MinIntervalMs;\n      the tracking map is capped
      so spoofed-IP floods can't exhaust memory."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
