  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.
    MemberName: MAX_COMPONENT
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 1
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Maximum quaternion component magnitude per bone slot.\n Components
      are quantized within [-maxComp, maxComp] instead of full [-0.707, 0.707].\n\n
      DESIGN: most joints use full InvSqrt2 range to support ALL human poses\n (dancing,
      gymnastics, sleeping, backbends, splits, etc.).\n Only joints that are physically
      incapable of large rotation get tighter ranges:\n   - Eyes: ~35\xB0 max look
      direction (anatomical limit of extraocular muscles)\n   - Jaw: ~40\xB0 max
      open + sideways (TMJ limit)\n   - Toes: ~55\xB0 max curl (metatarsal limit)\n  
      - UpperChest: ~50\xB0 max (thoracic vertebrae are fused/limited)\n\n Hips orientation
      is sent separately as a full-precision compressed quaternion,\n so upside-down,
      sideways, etc. are unaffected by these limits."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
